# Network Access Fixed

I have configured the application to allow access from your local network IP and ensured the server is running with the correct host flags.

## Changes Made

### Configuration Update
Updated [next.config.ts](file:///d:/TodoPro/next.config.ts) to include `allowedDevOrigins`. In Next.js 16.2.2, this is a top-level configuration required to allow development features like Hot Module Replacement (HMR) to work over the network.

```typescript
const nextConfig: NextConfig = {
  allowedDevOrigins: ["localhost", "172.16.11.21"],
};
```

### Server Restart
Restarted the server using the `npm run server` command, which executes `next dev -H 0.0.0.0`.

## Verification Results

- **Localhost**: `http://localhost:3000` (Working)
- **Network**: `http://172.16.11.21:3000` (Now allowed)

> [!TIP]
> If you still cannot access the app from another device, please check if your Windows Firewall is allowing incoming connections on port `3000`.
